{number: 108}
{title: The Solid Rock}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [C] hope is built on nothing less
Than [F] Jesus' blood and [G7] righteous-[C] ness;
I dare not trust the sweetest frame,
But [F] wholly lean on [G7] Jesus' [C] name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
On [C] Christ, the solid [F] Rock, I stand;
All [C] other ground is [G7] sinking sand,
All [C] other ground is [G7] sinking [C] sand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] darkness veils His lovely face,
I [F] rest on His un-[G7] changing [C] grace;
In every high and stormy gale,
My [F] anchor holds with-[G7] in the [C] veil.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
His [C] oath, His covenant, His blood,
Sup-[F] port me in the [G7] whelming [C] flood;
When all around my soul gives way,
He [F] then is all my [G7] hope and [C] stay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [C] He shall come with trumpet sound,
Oh, [F] may I then in [G7] Him be [C] found;
Dressed in His righteousness alone,
Fault-[F] less to stand be-[G7] fore the [C] throne.
{end_of_verse}
